@*
    The Razor parity twin's layout (D1; ledger entry E5).

    Like the Liquid/Scriban/Handlebars twins, this reproduces the byte sequence Heddle's
    home.heddle + layout.heddle actually emit — the reusable-section defaults, the fixed
    component outputs, and the ordered area menus — rather than transcribing the layout's
    literal HTML chrome. See Runners/README.md for why Heddle's output is that fragment
    sequence, and Runners/LiquidTemplates.cs for the same page in Liquid.

    Every value comes from the shared TwinContent fixtures via RazorTwinModel, so this twin
    cannot drift from the engine it is compared against. Html.Raw is used throughout because
    Heddle emits these fragments unencoded; Razor's default @ expression would HTML-encode
    them, which is the same reason the Handlebars twin uses triple mustaches.

    Whitespace here is free: the parity comparison unifies line endings, collapses runs of
    whitespace between tags, and then (contract v2 step N3b) strips every remaining whitespace
    run from both sides before the ordinal compare.
*@
@model Heddle.Performance.Runners.RazorTwinModel

@Html.Raw(Model.Sections["meta"])
@Html.Raw(Model.Sections["social"])

@Html.Raw(Model.Components["assets_styles"])
@Html.Raw(Model.Components["custom_styles"])
@Html.Raw(Model.Components["head_scripts"])
@Html.Raw(Model.Components["body_scripts"])

@* The navigation areas, in layout.heddle's order. *@
@for (var i = 0; i < Model.AreaOrder.Count - 1; i++)
{
    @Html.Raw(Model.Areas[Model.AreaOrder[i]])
}

@*
    layout.heddle's @body() slot sits here, between the last navigation area and the footer
    area. It resolves to the layout's empty default, so this renders nothing — but the slot is
    kept in its real position, and Razor requires a layout to call RenderBody exactly once.
*@
@RenderBody()

@* The footer area — the last entry in TwinContent.AreaOrder. *@
@Html.Raw(Model.Areas[Model.AreaOrder[Model.AreaOrder.Count - 1]])

@Html.Raw(Model.Components["assets_scripts"])
@Html.Raw(Model.Sections["page_scripts"])
@Html.Raw(Model.Sections["endpage_scripts"])
@Html.Raw(Model.Components["body_end_scripts"])
